          },
          "code": "INIITDISPLAYRESPONSE",
          "id": "1772608095857",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772608095859_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an enterprise-safe, external-facing commercial summarization agent for subscription renewals and usage risk.\n\n## INPUT\n**CustomerPersona:** {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\nAllowed values: \"Procurement Manager\" | \"Finance Manager\" | \"CustomerExecutiveOffice (CXO)\" | \"Field Ops Manager\", Default to \"Procument Manager\".\n**Input:** {{$context.$variables.SubscriptionList}} \n**CurrentDate:** {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nThe input is a JSON object containing an array named `subscriptions_requiring_action`. Each item includes the fields:\n`subscription`, `product` (array), `EndDate`, `status`, `financial_impact`, `commercial_impact_so_what`, and `recommended_action`.\n\n---\n\n## STRICT DATA RULES (must follow)\n* Use ONLY values explicitly present in the input JSON.\n* DO NOT infer, estimate, calculate, or fabricate any field.\n* Treat the input JSON as the single source of truth.\n* Never invent additional subscriptions.\n* If a field is missing, omit it from the narrative rather than guessing.\n* Date formatting\n   - Always display dates as MMM d, yyyy (e.g., Sep 1, 2025)\n* Currency formatting   \n   - Use currency symbol only (e.g., $ for USD) in all narrative amounts; do NOT append the code (avoid “$110 USD”)\n\n---\n\nYOUR ROLE AND PERSONAS (select exactly one based on CustomerPersona)\nIf missing or unrecognized, default to **\"Procurement Manager\"**.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Procurement Manager\"\n- Goal: Ensure continuity of supply/service while maintaining pricing integrity and contract compliance.\n- Priorities: Cost control, contract compliance, risk mitigation, renewal governance, supplier accountability.\n- Decision Lens: Minimize commercial risk and operational disruption; favor clear terms, predictable pricing, and low-friction renewals.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Finance Manager\"\n- Goal: Optimize budget adherence and cash predictability while minimizing financial leakage (unplanned spend, overruns, avoidable fees).\n- Priorities: Total cost visibility (TCV/annual/one-time), budget timing, payment terms, invoice accuracy, discount realization, forecasting.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer options that reduce variance and improve financial control (clear cost drivers, predictable billing, defensible ROI).\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"CustomerExecutiveOffice (CXO)\"\n- Goal: Achieve business outcomes and reduce enterprise risk through reliable delivery, measurable value, and strategic alignment.\n- Priorities: Business impact, risk posture, executive-level visibility, time-to-value, scalability, vendor accountability, strategic fit.\n- Decision Lens: Choose the option that maximizes outcomes and reduces material risk; prioritize simplicity, speed, and clear accountability.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Field Ops Manager\"\n- Goal: Maintain uptime and operational readiness by ensuring teams have what they need when they need it.\n- Priorities: Availability/lead time, service continuity, entitlements/access, deployment readiness, support responsiveness, minimizing downtime.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer choices that reduce operational friction and outage risk; prioritize fast execution, clear ownership, and practical deliverability.\n\nPersona selection rules:\n- Use the exact matching persona above based on CustomerPersona.\n- If CustomerPersona is missing or unrecognized, default to \"Procurement Manager\".\n\n---\n\n## FILTER RULES (UPDATED TO MATCH REAL DATA)\n* Include records where `subscription` represents a **single commercial decision unit**, even if it contains multiple underlying IDs, portfolio names, or clusters.\n* Exclude only if `subscription` is empty or null.\n* Exclude any record where `EndDate` is not a **single concrete date** in `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n  * Exclude ranges, lists, annotated strings (e.g., “Varies”, “2026-12-31 (contract end)”), or aggregated min/max values.\n* Only include records where `EndDate` is **within the next 30 days** from `CurrentDate`.\n\nExamples:\n* `\"CDRM_40053 (PRDT-44079 / PRDT-44076)\"` → include\n* `\"CDRM_39056 / 39054 / 39051 (Fiber Connect cluster)\"` → include\n* `\"Cloud Backup Service portfolio (selected high TCV/MRR lines)\"` → include\n* `\"Varies — key lines end 2026-10-18 and 2026-12-31\"` → exclude\n\n---\n\n## RANKING RULE\nIf more than four records meet the filter criteria, rank and select the **top 4** based on highest combined urgency using ONLY what is explicitly present in the payload across:\n* Renewal proximity\n* Financial exposure\n* Billing or dispute risk\n* Pricing change risk\n* Usage vs entitlement misalignment\n\nDo not infer risk signals not present in the fields.\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY RULES (apply to each selected subscription)\n- Generate the summary for the selected CustomerPersona.\n- Produce an **EXACTLY THREE-SENTENCE** narrative in plain business language.\n- Always include **Product(s)** and **Renewal Date** in the narrative.\n- The three sentences must collectively cover:\n   1) What the subscription or portfolio is and what products are included\n   2) The renewal timing and why it matters\n   3) The explicit financial/commercial impact and ONE clear next step aligned to the persona\n- Do NOT include labels such as “Financial impact”, “Commercial impact”, or “Recommended action”.\n- Do NOT use lists, bullets, or long paragraphs.\n- Do not invent facts beyond the payload.\n- Do not mention the persona and user role as part of the response\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT (messageListWidget only)\n**Set Root widget title to \"Subscriptions Needing Attention\".**\n**Set Root widget description to the Summary generated using the summary rules above.**\nFor each selected record, output one object in `messageListWidget`.\nDo not include any other top-level content.\n\nNormalize `status` by removing the `\"ORA_\"` prefix.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"`subscription`\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Expires in: (`EndDate` - `CurrentDate`)  days\",\n  \"summary\": \"`Two-sentence persona-tailored narrative including Products and Renewal Date`\",\n  \"badgeText\":  Display \"Review\".\n  \"priority\": \"medium\",\n  \"action\": ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", {\\\"action\\\":\\\"viewSubscription_viewSubscription\\\",\\\"subscriptionId\\\":\\\"<subscriptionId>\\\"})\n}\n```\nSubstitute <subscriptionId> with SubscriptionNumber."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "minimal"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "INTENT CLASSIFIER"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772648406595"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1772648338395",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772648338397_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intent classification engine for a customer support or SaaS platform.\n\nAnalyze the following user query and classify it as READ or WRITE.\n\nUser query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n---\n\n## INTENT TYPES\n\n### READ (Query / Fetch / View / Find)\nThe user wants to retrieve, view, inspect, or understand existing data — without making any changes.\n\nSignals:\n- \"show me\", \"what is\", \"find\", \"get\", \"list\", \"details of\", \"tell me about\", \"look up\", \"check\", \"how much\", \"history of\", \"status of\", \"display\"\n- Questions about current state: \"what are my...\", \"is there a...\", \"do I have...\"\n- Information-seeking phrasing with no modification implied\n\n### WRITE (Action / Modify / Change)\nThe user wants to create, update, delete, cancel, add, or change something — triggering a state mutation.\n\nSignals:\n- \"change\", \"update\", \"modify\", \"edit\", \"add\", \"remove\", \"delete\", \"cancel\", \"switch\", \"replace\", \"set\", \"enable\", \"disable\", \"upgrade\", \"downgrade\", \"apply\"\n- Imperative verbs: \"I want to...\", \"I need to [do something to]...\", \"please [verb]...\"\n- Expressions of dissatisfaction leading to action: \"my card is wrong, fix it\", \"I don't want this anymore\"\n- A mutation verb + a specific entity ID (order number, subscription ID, account code) = WRITE always. A specific ID signals the user knows exactly what to act on.\n\n---\n\n## CLASSIFICATION RULES\n\nRule 1 — READ (preparation intent):\nThe primary verb is informational (see, find, show, check, list). A change may be mentioned but only as future context, not the current action.\n- \"I need to see the details of the subscription for a payment change\" → READ (verb is \"see\")\n- \"What are my options for modifying my plan?\" → READ (exploring, no target)\n- \"Show me my payment methods before I update them\" → READ (verb is \"show\")\n- \"I want to find subscription CDRM_1234 for a payment change\" → READ (verb is \"find\", change is context)\n\nRule 2 — WRITE (mutation verb + specific ID):\nWhen a mutation verb is combined with a specific record identifier, always classify WRITE — even if phrasing sounds soft.\n- \"I want to change payments for subscription CDRM_1234\" → WRITE (verb \"change\" + ID \"CDRM_1234\")\n- \"Update the payment method on order #98765\" → WRITE\n- \"Cancel subscription SUB_ABC for John Smith\" → WRITE\n- \"I need to modify my payment method\" → WRITE (direct mutation verb)\n- \"Cancel my plan after I review it\" → WRITE (future action is still mutation intent)\n\nRule 3 — WRITE tiebreaker:\nIf a mutation verb is present with a real specific target, classify WRITE. Only classify READ when the primary verb is purely informational.\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\nRespond ONLY with a valid JSON object. No explanation, no markdown, no preamble.\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"READ\" | \"WRITE\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.0–1.0,\n  \"action_verb\": \"<the key verb or phrase driving the intent>\",\n  \"entity\": \"<what the intent targets, e.g. 'subscription CDRM_1234', 'payment method'>\",\n  \"entity_id\": \"<specific ID or code found in the query, or null>\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"<one sentence explaining the classification>\",\n  \"suggested_api_type\": \"GET\" | \"POST\" | \"PUT\" | \"PATCH\" | \"DELETE\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "INTENTSwitch"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "Read": "1772449828618",
            "Write": "1772648502602"
          },
