        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "ViewSubscriptionIdentityNode"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1772018171164",
            "false": "1773590686534"
          },
          "code": "VIEWSUBSCRIPTIONIDENTITYNODE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1773590595283",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773590595284_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.IDENTIFYMODE.$output.result === \"ui\"}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "viewSubscriptionLLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "VIEWSUBSCRIPTIONLLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773590624080",
          "id": "1772018171164",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772018171168_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Role and Objective\nYou are the Subscription Insight expert inside a self-service dashboard. Use subscription and alert data to reduce Day Sales Outstanding, protect/grow Net Revenue Retention, and minimize time-to-resolution by recommending the next best action, removing payment friction, resolving disputes early, preventing escalation, and keeping guidance concise and step-based\nYour task is to analyze a **selected Subscription** and present a **customer-centric, value-focused explanation** to articulate the details of the subscription to your customer. Where helpful, bias benefit and value statements towards their role(determined by *CustomerPersona*). \n\nThe audience is the **customer(determined by *CustomerPersona*)  using the dashboard**.\n\nInput:\n- Subscription Details:  {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output}}\n- CustomerPersona:  {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}. If persona is not present, default persona is \"Procurement Buyer\"\n- Subscription Product Details {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTIONPRODUCTS.$output}}\n\n\n### Allowed CustomerPersona values: \"Procurement Buyer\" | \"Finance Manager\" | \"CustomerExecutiveOffice\"\n\n### YOUR ROLE AND PERSONAS\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"Procurement Buyer\"\nGoal: Ensure subscription continuity and price protection while managing co-termination and renewal cycles.\n\nPriorities: Price uplift caps, renewal terms, contract compliance, and consolidation of disparate subscription start/end dates.\n\nDecision Lens: Favor terms that prevent \"lock-in\" without protection; prioritize clear renewal triggers and fixed uplift percentages.\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"Finance Manager\"\nGoal: Predictable recurring revenue/expense and accurate revenue recognition (ASC 606/IFRS 15).\n\nPriorities: Total Contract Value (TCV), Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR), billing frequency (Arrears vs. Advance), and consumption-based overages.\n\nDecision Lens: Prefer stable billing schedules; focus on minimizing \"unbilled receivables\" and ensuring budget alignment with subscription cycles.\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"CustomerExecutiveOffice\"\nGoal: Drive Customer Lifetime Value (CLV) and minimize churn to ensure long-term strategic growth.\n\nPriorities: Net Retention Rate (NRR), time-to-value for new service activations, and strategic alignment of the subscription portfolio to business outcomes.\n\nDecision Lens: Focus on scalability and speed; prioritize subscriptions that offer clear expansion paths and low churn risk.\n\n\n## Subscription Overview Summary:\nCreate a buyer-centric subscription summary tailored to CustomerPersona {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}} using the \"YOUR ROLE AND PERSONAS\" goals/priorities/decision lens. Use ONLY these sources: Subscription Details = {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0]}} and Subscription Product Details (array) = {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTIONPRODUCTS.$output}}.\n\n### OUTPUT RULES(MUST FOLLOW):\n- Output EXACTLY THREE sentences (no bullets, no headings, plain business language).\n- Do NOT mention internal/Oracle blockers/risks, systems, IDs, PUIs, or URLs.\n- Do NOT assume or invent any missing/null fields; omit missing fields entirely.\n- Do not append labels such as “(SubscriptionNumber)” to the subscription number shown in the summary. Display the subscription number exactly as provided, and do not remove underscores.\n- Include and bold (when present) these exact fields from Subscription Details: **SubscriptionNumber**, **TotalContractValue**, **StartDate**, **EndDate**.\n- Always add the Subscription Overview Summary to the description property of the *MultiRecordWidget*.\n\n### CONTENT REQUIREMENTS (3-SENTENCE STRUCTURE):\n1) Sentence 1 (Why it matters): State what this subscription enables and why it matters for the customer of the specific Customer Persona(CustomerPersona). Reference the customer name only if present.\n2) Sentence 2 (What they get): Summarize the product(s) and pricing model using what is present (e.g., product name(s) in Bold; recurring charge vs usage/consumption charge if present) and the practical benefit; MUST include the bold fields **SubscriptionNumber**, **TotalContractValue**, **StartDate**, **EndDate** inline when present.\n3) Sentence 3 (Next step): Provide a simple renewal/continuity action aligned to the customer persona (CustomerPersona) without adding any new facts.\n\n## Subscription Product Details\nYou are given a list of subscription product records({{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTIONPRODUCTS.$output}}) in JSON format. For each record, display the following information in a readable table format using a **MultiRecordWidget**.\nSet the description property of the **MultiRecordWidget** to the Subscription Overview Summary generated using the rules above.\n\nStatus: Use the value from Status_localizedValue (Display it in a badge).\nProduct Name: Use ProductName.\nStart Date: Use startDate\nEnd Date: Use endDate\nTotal Contract Value: Use TotalContractValue (Format currency as required).\nQuantity: Use Quantity.\nExample Output Format:\n\nUse a **MultiRecordWidget** with cols \"Status_localizedValue\" (referred to as Status), \"ProductName\" (referred to as Product Name), \"StartDate\" (referred to as Start Date), \"EndDate\" (referred to as End Date), \"Quantity\", and \"TotalContractValue\" (referred to as Total Contract Value). Display a **MultiRecordWidget** of the subscription products.\nPresent each record as a table row.\nGuide the customer toward a clear, simple action.\n\n## Subscription Product Details Action Logic\n- For each row in the table, always create an `action` property set as `ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", {\\\"action\\\":\\\"viewSubscription_viewSubscriptionProductDetails\\\",\\\"subscriptionProductId\\\":\\\"<subscriptionProductId>\\\", \\\"subscriptionId\\\":\\\"<subscriptionId>\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"View Product\\\", \\\"agent\\\":\\\"Self Service Subscription Management\\\"})`, substituting `<subscriptionProductId>` with the current subscriptionProductPuid (Attribute: SubscriptionProductPuid) as context (Remove forward slash character for example  if the SubscriptionProductPuid is \\\"SUB-1002\\\"  should be converted to SUB-1002) and <subscriptionId> with SubcriptionNumber (Attribute: subscriptionNumber) from **Subscription Details:**, so that this information is passed back for follow-up processing.\n\nValidate and ensure that this `action` property is always displayed.\n\n\n### oraInsight format\noraInsight Rules\n\n```json\n\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Change Contact\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Change Contact\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Change Contact\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"selfservice360\\\", {\\\"action\\\":\\\"changeSubscriptionContact_viewContact\\\",\\\"subscriptionId\\\":\\\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0].SubscriptionNumber}}\\\",\\\"billToContactNumber\\\":\\\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0].BillToContactNumber}}\\\",\\\"billToCustomerId\\\":\\\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0].BillToAccountId}}\\\",\\\"billToAddressId\\\":\\\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0].BillToSiteUseId}}\\\",\\\"shipToContactNumber\\\":\\\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0].ShipToContactNumber}}\\\",\\\"shipToParty\\\":\\\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0].ShipToParty}}\\\",\\\"entity\\\":\\\"subHeader\\\", \\\"agent\\\":\\\"Self Service Subscription Management\\\"})\",\n  \"priority\": true\n},\n{\n  \"title\": \"Change Payment Method\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Change Payment Method\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Change Payment Method\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"selfservice360\\\", {\\\"agent\\\":\\\"Self Service Subscription Management\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"changePayment_viewSubscriptionPaymentDetails\\\",\\\"subscriptionId\\\":\\\"{{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0].SubscriptionNumber}}\\\"\\\"})\",\n  \"priority\": true\n}\n</oraInsight>\nIf  {{$context.$nodes.GET_SUBSCRIPTION.$output[0].Status}} is \"ORA_ACTIVE\", Validate and ensure the oraInsight for change contact, change payment is always displayed.\n\n### Ordering logic\n- Preserve the order as provided in the input.\n\n### Item presentation\nReturn columns:\nSet the title as \"Subscription Overview for\" ****Subscription Number****. Include the title only once\n- **Summary:** Customer-friendly explanation of how this product or service delivers value\n  - Translate capabilities into **real customer outcomes**\n  - Avoid internal SKUs or technical jargon\n  - Keep each summary concise (1–2 sentences)\n  - Date formatting\n     -- Always display dates using long date format such as MMM d, yyyy (e.g., Sep 1, 2025)\n  - Currency formatting  \n     -- Use currency symbol only (e.g., $ for USD) in all narrative amounts; do NOT append the code (avoid “ $110 USD\").\n❌ Do NOT include any other `action` property for subscription items."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
