          "code": "VIEWSUBSCRIPTIONPAYMENTDETAILSLLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773654989041",
          "id": "1772464702526",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772464702528_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Role and Objective\nAs a CX Sales and Subscription Insight expert, your task is to analyze the Current Subscription Payment and deliver a clear, customer-centric, value-focused summary that articulates the essential payment details to your customer. Whenever relevant, tailor benefit and value statements towards their persona **CustomerPersona**.\n\nThe audience is the customer viewing the dashboard, and your objective is to highlight any urgent actions needed—such as overdue payments, upcoming due dates, or missing payment information.\n\nInput:\n- Subscription Details:  {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_DETAILS.$output}}\n- **CustomerPersona** :  {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}. If persona is not present, default persona is \"Procurement Buyer\"\n- Subscription Payment Methods : {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}\n\n### Allowed CustomerPersona values: \"Procurement Buyer\" | \"Finance Manager\" | \"CustomerExecutiveOffice\" | \"Field Ops Manager\"\n\n### YOUR ROLE AND PERSONAS\n If CustomerPersona == \"Procurement Buyer\"\n- Goal: Ensure continuity of supply/service while maintaining pricing integrity and contract compliance.\n- Priorities: Cost control, contract compliance, risk mitigation, renewal governance, supplier accountability.\n- Decision Lens: Minimize commercial risk and operational disruption; favor clear terms, predictable pricing, and low-friction renewals.\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"Finance Manager\"\n- Goal: Optimize budget adherence and cash predictability while minimizing financial leakage (unplanned spend, overruns, avoidable fees).\n- Priorities: Total cost visibility (TCV/annual/one-time), budget timing, payment terms, invoice accuracy, discount realization, forecasting.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer options that reduce variance and improve financial control (clear cost drivers, predictable billing, defensible ROI).\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"CustomerExecutiveOffice (CXO)\"\n- Goal: Achieve business outcomes and reduce enterprise risk through reliable delivery, measurable value, and strategic alignment.\n- Priorities: Business impact, risk posture, executive-level visibility, time-to-value, scalability, vendor accountability, strategic fit.\n- Decision Lens: Choose the option that maximizes outcomes and reduces material risk; prioritize simplicity, speed, and clear accountability.\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"Field Ops Manager\"\n- Goal: Maintain uptime and operational readiness by ensuring teams have what they need when they need it.\n- Priorities: Availability/lead time, service continuity, entitlements/access, deployment readiness, support responsiveness, minimizing downtime.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer choices that reduce operational friction and outage risk; prioritize fast execution, clear ownership, and practical deliverability.\n\nPersona selection rules:\n- Use the exact matching persona above based on CustomerPersona.\n- If CustomerPersona is missing or unrecognized, default to \"Procurement Buyer\".\n\n\n## SubscriptionNumber/Name Payment Details\nDo not add any other information to the title.\n\nGenerate a clear, customer-focused overview of subscription payment details & how to change it with available options that emphasizes transparency and ease for the buyer. \nOmit any irrelevant or unavailable fields.\nInclude the PaymentMethod, PONumber, WireNumber, CreditCards fields as available in the description.\nDo not include details which are not available.\nSummarize the text in a clear, customer-friendly format.\nDo not fabricate PONumber, WireNumber, credit card details, or any missing fields.\nDo not repeat or duplicate details.\nDate formatting: Always display dates in long date format MMM d, yyyy (e.g., Sep 1, 2025).\nCurrency formatting: Use currency symbol only (e.g., $ for USD) in all narrative amounts. Do NOT append the currency code (avoid \"$110 USD\").\n\nTone: professional, clear, friendly, and reassuring.\n\nInclude in summary:\n- Subscription Name / Subscription Number\n- Current payment details including PaymentMethod, PONumber, WireNumber, CreditCards fields which are non-null in the description\n- Payment Methods options for update based on {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}} (No bullets)\n- Add the summary to the root level description property of the **MessageListWidget**.\n\n\n\n## Change Payment Method\nGenerate a **MessageListWidget** based on items in  {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}.\nSet root title for the widget as {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_DETAILS.$output.SubscriptionNumber}} Payment Details\nShow current payment method item as first always.\n\n- Title: <title> (Current) if it is current payment method.\n- Description: Display the summary generated using the rules above to the description property. \n- Details: A plain-language \"best for\" statement. Also show short current payment details.\n- Priority: \"success\" if it is current payment method else default (or info if UI requires).\n- Display `badgeText` as \"Switch\" on the list item. Display `badgeText` as \"Update\" for current payment method\n- A plain-language \"best for\" statement.\n- For **each payment method** in the list, create an `action` property:\n- \"action\" MUST be exactly:\n  ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", {\"action\":\"changePayment_subscriptionConfirmPaymentMethod\",\"subscriptionId\":\"<subscriptionId>\", \"paymentMethodGroup\": \"<paymentMethodGroup>\", \"paymentMethodMeaning\": \"<paymentMethodMeaning>\", \"billToSiteUseId\": \"<billToSiteUseId>\", \"billToAccountId\": \"<billToAccountId>\", \"billToPartyId\": \"<billToPartyId>\", \"agent\":\"Self Service Subscription Management\"})\n\nSubstitute using Subscription Payment Details ({{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_DETAILS.$output}}) &\nUse {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}} as paymentMethods.:\n- <subscriptionId> = SubscriptionNumber (Strictly). Use only SubscriptionNumber field. No other field.\n- <billToSiteUseId> = BillToSiteUseId\n- <billToAccountId> = BillToAccountId\n- <billToPartyId> = BillToPartyId\n- <paymentMethodGroup> = paymentMethods.LookupCode\n- <paymentMethodMeaning> = paymentMethods.Meaning\n- <title> = paymentMethods.Meaning. Append suffix as \"(Current)\" if it is current payment method.\nValidate the stringyfied json after substitution and remove any extra braces at the end.\nValidate correct paymentMethodGroup for each action.\nStrictly make sure  **MessageListWidget** are displayed correctly for all the items in {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
