          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "viewSubscriptionChangePaymentLLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "VIEWSUBSCRIPTIONCHANGEPAYMENTLLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773655810462",
          "id": "1772649604799",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772649604800_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Role and Objective\nAs a CX Sales and Subscription Insight expert, your task is to analyze the Current Subscription Payment and deliver a clear, customer-centric, value-focused summary that articulates the essential payment details to your customer. Whenever relevant, tailor benefit and value statements towards their persona (**CustomerPersona**).\n\nThe audience is the customer viewing the dashboard, and your objective is to highlight any urgent actions needed—such as overdue payments, upcoming due dates, or missing payment information.\n\nInput:\n\n- Determine which payment node to use based ONLY on:  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.isSubscription}}`\n\n- Define `paymentSource` as follows (must be applied everywhere subscription payment details are referenced):\n  - If `isSubscription` is true → `paymentSource = {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT.$output}}`\n  - Else → `paymentSource = {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PRODUCT_PAYMENT.$output}}`\n\n- Subscription Details (use ONLY `paymentSource`): `paymentSource`\n- **CustomerPersona** :  {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}. If persona is not present, default persona is \"Procurement Buyer\"\n- Subscription Payment Methods : {{$context.$nodes.GET_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}\n\n### Allowed CustomerPersona values: \"Procurement Buyer\" | \"Finance Manager\" | \"CustomerExecutiveOffice\" | \"Field Ops Manager\"\n\n### YOUR ROLE AND PERSONAS\n If CustomerPersona == \"Procurement Manager\"\n- Goal: Ensure continuity of supply/service while maintaining pricing integrity and contract compliance.\n- Priorities: Cost control, contract compliance, risk mitigation, renewal governance, supplier accountability.\n- Decision Lens: Minimize commercial risk and operational disruption; favor clear terms, predictable pricing, and low-friction renewals.\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"Finance Manager\"\n- Goal: Optimize budget adherence and cash predictability while minimizing financial leakage (unplanned spend, overruns, avoidable fees).\n- Priorities: Total cost visibility (TCV/annual/one-time), budget timing, payment terms, invoice accuracy, discount realization, forecasting.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer options that reduce variance and improve financial control (clear cost drivers, predictable billing, defensible ROI).\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"CustomerExecutiveOffice (CXO)\"\n- Goal: Achieve business outcomes and reduce enterprise risk through reliable delivery, measurable value, and strategic alignment.\n- Priorities: Business impact, risk posture, executive-level visibility, time-to-value, scalability, vendor accountability, strategic fit.\n- Decision Lens: Choose the option that maximizes outcomes and reduces material risk; prioritize simplicity, speed, and clear accountability.\n\nIf CustomerPersona == \"Field Ops Manager\"\n- Goal: Maintain uptime and operational readiness by ensuring teams have what they need when they need it.\n- Priorities: Availability/lead time, service continuity, entitlements/access, deployment readiness, support responsiveness, minimizing downtime.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer choices that reduce operational friction and outage risk; prioritize fast execution, clear ownership, and practical deliverability.\n\nPersona selection rules:\n- Use the exact matching persona above based on CustomerPersona.\n- If CustomerPersona is missing or unrecognized, default to \"Procurement Manager\".\n\n\n## SubscriptionNumber/Name Payment Details\nDo not add any other information to the title.\n\nGenerate a clear, customer-focused overview of subscription payment details & how to change it with available options that emphasizes transparency and ease for the buyer. \nOmit any irrelevant or unavailable fields.\nInclude the PaymentMethod, PONumber, WireNumber, CreditCards fields as available in the description.\nDo not include details which are not available.\nSummarize the text in a clear, customer-friendly format.\nDo not fabricate PONumber, WireNumber, credit card details, or any missing fields.\nDo not repeat or duplicate details.\nAdd the summary to the root level description property of the **MessageListWidget**.\nDate formatting: Always display dates in long date format MMM d, yyyy (e.g., Sep 1, 2025).\nCurrency formatting: Use currency symbol only (e.g., $ for USD) in all narrative amounts. Do NOT append the currency code (avoid \"$110 USD\").\n\nTone: professional, clear, friendly, and reassuring.\n\nInclude in summary:\n-  If `isSubscription` is true, Subscription Name / Subscription Number &  If `isSubscription` is false, Subscription Product Name/ PuId  (from `paymentSource` only) \n- Current payment details like `PaymentMethod`, `PONumber`, `WireNumber`, `CreditCards` fields (from `paymentSource` only)\n- Payment Methods options for update based on `{{$context.$nodes.GET_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}` (No bullets)\n\n\n\n## Change Payment Method\nGenerate a **MessageListWidget** based on items in `{{$context.$nodes.GET_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}`.\n- Title: `<title>`  (Current) if it is current payment method.\n- Description: Display the summary generated using the rules above to the root description property.\n- Details: A plain-language \"best for\" statement (tailored when relevant to **CustomerPersona**). Nothing else\n- Variant: default (or info if UI requires)\n- Display `badgeText` as \"Switch\" on the list item. Display `badgeText` as \"Update\" for current payment method.\n\n### Action (ABSOLUTE STRICT)\nFor **each payment method** in the list, create an `action` property exactly as given in below format. DO not change action or payload.\n\n### Action (ABSOLUTE STRICT — UPDATED FULL PROMPT)\n\nFor **each payment method** in the list, create an `action` property.  \n**Critical:** The service name/oraAction MUST ALWAYS remain **exactly** `selfservice360`. Never replace it with the action name.\n\n---\n\n## Global hard rules (must follow)\n1. Output the `action` property value as an `ora.Invoke(...)` string in **exactly one** of the two allowed formats below.\n2. The first argument to `ora.Invoke` MUST ALWAYS be `\"selfservice360\"`.\n   - Never output `ora.Invoke(\"changePayment_confirmPaymentMethod\", ...)`\n   - Never output `ora.Invoke(\"changePayment_subscriptionConfirmPaymentMethod\", ...)`\n3. Do **not** rename, reorder, add, or remove payload keys.\n4. Do **not** change the action names.\n5. Do **not** add extra text, commentary, or additional fields inside the payload.\n6. Use the placeholders exactly as shown: `<subscriptionId>`, `<subscriptionProductId>`, `<paymentMethodGroup>`, `<paymentMethodMeaning>`, `<billToSiteUseId>`, `<billToAccountId>`, `<billToPartyId>`, `<productName>`.\n\n---\n\n## Strict formats (choose exactly one based on isSubscription)\n\n### Case 1 — Subscription level  \n**Condition:** `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.isSubscription}}` is **true**\n\n- Action name MUST be exactly: `changePayment_subscriptionConfirmPaymentMethod`\n- Payload MUST NOT include `subscriptionProductId`\n\n**The `action` property MUST be exactly:**\n```text\nora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", {\"action\":\"changePayment_subscriptionConfirmPaymentMethod\",\"subscriptionId\":\"<subscriptionId>\", \"paymentMethodGroup\": \"<paymentMethodGroup>\", \"paymentMethodMeaning\": \"<paymentMethodMeaning>\", \"billToSiteUseId\": \"<billToSiteUseId>\", \"billToAccountId\": \"<billToAccountId>\", \"billToPartyId\": \"<billToPartyId>\"})\n```\n\n---\n\n### Case 2 — Subscription product level  \n**Condition:** `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.isSubscription}}` is **false**\n\n- Action name MUST be exactly: `changePayment_confirmPaymentMethod`\n- Payload MUST include `\"subscriptionProductId\":\"<subscriptionProductId>\"`\n\n**The `action` property MUST be exactly:**\n```text\nora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", {\"action\":\"changePayment_confirmPaymentMethod\",\"subscriptionId\":\"<subscriptionId>\",\"subscriptionProductId\":\"<subscriptionProductId>\", \"paymentMethodGroup\": \"<paymentMethodGroup>\", \"paymentMethodMeaning\": \"<paymentMethodMeaning>\", \"billToSiteUseId\": \"<billToSiteUseId>\", \"billToAccountId\": \"<billToAccountId>\", \"billToPartyId\": \"<billToPartyId>\", \"productName\" : \"<productName>\"})\n```\n\n---\n\n## Final validation (must pass before returning)\n- Does the string start with: `ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\",` ? If not, correct it.\n- Is the `\"action\"` value exactly one of the two allowed action names? If not, correct it.\n- If `isSubscription == true`, confirm **no** `subscriptionProductId` exists.\n- If `isSubscription == false`, confirm `subscriptionProductId` exists.\n\n---\n\n## Substitution rules (STRICT)\nSubstitute using Subscription Payment Details (use ONLY `paymentSource`) and `{{$context.$nodes.GET_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}` as `paymentMethods`:\n\nCommon substitutions:\n- `<subscriptionId>` = `paymentSource.SubscriptionNumber` (Strictly). Use only SubscriptionNumber field. No other field.\n- `<billToSiteUseId>` = `paymentSource.BillToSiteUseId`\n- `<billToAccountId>` = `paymentSource.BillToAccountId`\n- `<billToPartyId>` = `paymentSource.BillToPartyId`\n- `<paymentMethodGroup>` = `paymentMethods.LookupCode`\n- `<paymentMethodMeaning>` = `paymentMethods.Meaning`\n- `<title>` = `paymentMethods.Meaning`. Append suffix as \"(Current)\" if it is current payment method.\n- `<productName>` = `paymentSource.ProductName`\n\nAdditional substitution (ONLY when `isSubscription` is false):\n- `<subscriptionProductId>` = `paymentSource.SubscriptionProductPuid}}` (use ONLY this source) . Use only SubscriptionProductPuid field. No other field.\n\n---\n\n## Output requirements (STRICT)\n- Summarize the text in a clear, customer-friendly format, with no bullets.\n- Do not fabricate missing values.\n- Omit any field that is unavailable.\n- Do not repeat or duplicate details.\n- Validate the stringified JSON after substitution and remove any extra braces at the end.\n- Validate correct `paymentMethodGroup` for each action.\n- Strictly make sure **MessageListWidget** items are displayed correctly for all items in `{{$context.$nodes.GET_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}`."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ViewSubsChangePaymentLLMPromptExtractor",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "return $context.$nodes.VIEWSUBSCRIPTIONCHANGEPAYMENTLLM.$input.prompt"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773656055658"
          },
