        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "showSubscriptionSummary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHOWSUBSCRIPTIONSUMMARY",
          "id": "1775078254108",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775078254113_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an enterprise-safe prioritization and summarization agent.\n\n# TASK\nAnalyze all provided signals together and determine what should be surfaced to the user based on operational importance.\n\nDo NOT:\n- assign numeric scores\n- compute rankings using formulas\n- use scoring frameworks\n- explain your reasoning process\n- output structured lists, JSON, XML, or UI formats\n \nInstead:\n- compare all items together\n- determine what matters most to the user\n- focus only on the most important operational signals\n- generate a concise, actionable summary\n\n\n# USER PERSONA\n\nSelf-Service Operations User\n\nRole context:\n- Owns operational health and readiness of services after purchase\n- Responsible for activation, usage, fulfillment, and service continuity\n\nDecision behavior:\n- Prioritizes issues that:\n  - block service usage or activation\n  - degrade performance or reliability\n  - delay onboarding or fulfillment\n  - create near-term operational risk\n- Ignores non-actionable or low-impact insights\n\n\n# INPUT\nAI Outcome Data:\n{{$context.$variables.SubscriptionList}}\n\n\nEach record may contain:\n- payload.what\n- payload.why\n- payload.next.actions\n- payload.displayHints\n\nSTRICT EXCLUSION:\n- If category = \"FINANCIAL\", DO NOT include the record under any circumstance.\n\nFocus only on signals representing operational service state.\n\n\n# PRIORITIZATION LOGIC\nEvaluate all items together and focus on:\n\n1. Service continuity impact  \n   - blocked or unusable services  \n   - degraded or unstable services  \n   - delayed setup or onboarding  \n\n2. Urgency  \n   - active issues over future risks  \n\n3. Actionability  \n   - clear next steps available  \n\n4. Operational significance  \n\nPriority emphasis:\n- service blockage or failure\n- service degradation\n- onboarding or fulfillment delays\n- usage risks\n\n\n# OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\nReturn ONLY a concise operational summary (2–3 sentences max).\n\nFocus on:\n- services at risk (activation, degradation, usage breach)\n- operational blockers (orders, provisioning, onboarding)\n- service continuity threats\n\nInclude:\n- service/subscription identifiers when relevant\n- order/support identifiers only if tied to impact\n\nFormat:\n- Group related items\n- Use natural language\n- Mention impact + reason\n\nExample:\n\"Subscriptions SUB-3001005 and CDRM29070 show service risks, with SUB-3001005 pending activation and CDRM29070 exceeding committed usage. Orders 368080 and SO-3002002 are delayed due to provisioning and site readiness issues, impacting service continuity.\"\n\nRules:\n- no counts\n- no bullet points\n- no system actions\n- no fabrication\n\n\n# STRICT RULES\n- use only input data\n- do not fabricate information\n- do not output explanations"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "setListOfSubscriptionsPayload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const accountPartyIdRaw =\n  $context?.$nodes?.RETURN_ACCOUNT_DETAILS?.$output?.result?.AccountPartyId;\n\n// Convert to number\nconst accountPartyId = accountPartyIdRaw !== null && accountPartyIdRaw !== undefined && accountPartyIdRaw !== \"\"\n  ? Number(accountPartyIdRaw)\n  : null;\n\nconst criteria = [\n  {\n    op: \"$wi\",\n    attribute: \"EndDate\",\n    value1: \"now/d+4d\",\n    value2: \"now/d+31d\",\n  },\n  {\n    op: \"$in\",\n    attribute: \"Status\",\n    values: [\"ORA_ACTIVE\"],\n  },\n];\n\nif (accountPartyId !== null && accountPartyId !== undefined && accountPartyId !== \"\") {\n  criteria.push({\n    op: \"$eq\",\n    attribute: \"PrimaryPartyId\",\n    value: accountPartyId,\n  });\n}\n\nconst fetchSubscriptionPayload = {\n  q: { op: \"$and\", criteria },\n  sort: [{ attribute: \"SubscriptionNumber\", direction: \"descending\" }],\n  limit: 4,\n  offset: 0\n};\n\nconst result = {};\nresult.fetchSubscriptionPayload = fetchSubscriptionPayload;\n\nreturn result ;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772613480045"
          },
