          "code": "CONFIRM_PRODUCT_CREDIT_CARD_PAYMENT_METHOD",
          "id": "1775070789043",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775070789045_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a single-sentence confirmation that the payment method change for subscription {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_PRODUCT_CREDIT_CARD_PAYMENT.$output.ProductName}} is completed.\n\nUse ONLY these fields from {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_PRODUCT_CREDIT_CARD_PAYMENT.$output}}: creditCards[0]. If WireNumber, PONumber, or creditCards[0] is null or empty, omit them entirely. Do not include any other fields. Do not infer values from the presence of other fields. Do not interpret or guess.\n\nStrict selection rule:\n\n- Determine the payment method SOLELY from PaymentMethod. Do NOT use creditCards or any other fields to decide the method.\n\nMap PaymentMethod to these human names exactly:\n\n- ORA_CREDIT_CARD → Credit card\n\nInclude method-specific details ONLY when the PaymentMethod matches and the detail exists:\n\n- Credit card: include details from creditCards[0] only if PaymentMethod = ORA_CREDIT_CARD. Exclude expiry date. Prefer Brand and last 4 if present (e.g., \"Visa ending 4242\"). If one is missing, show only what exists without guessing.\n\nFormatting:\n\n- One sentence. No bullets. No code formatting. Human-friendly names only. No expiry dates.\n\nStructure: \"Payment method for {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_PRODUCT_CREDIT_CARD_PAYMENT.$output.ProductName}} has been updated to [Human Payment Method Name][ with specific detail if present].\" If the method is unknown, use: \"Payment method for {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_PRODUCT_CREDIT_CARD_PAYMENT.$output.ProductName}} has been updated.\"\n\nValidation:\n\n- Use only values present in {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_PRODUCT_CREDIT_CARD_PAYMENT.$output}}. Exclude any field that is null or empty. Do not add or infer anything.\n- Ensure the chosen method is strictly the one from PaymentMethod; do not switch to Credit card unless PaymentMethod = ORA_CREDIT_CARD.\n\nExample with your sample data (do not copy values unless present at runtime):\n\"Payment method for Supremo Power Monitoring - Commercial has been updated to Credit card with Visa ending 7896.\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
