          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772048885508_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Generate a single-sentence confirmation that the payment method change for subscription {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHOD.$output.ProductName}} is completed.\n\nUse ONLY these fields from {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHOD.$output}}: PaymentMethod, WireNumber, PONumber. If WireNumber or PONumber is null or empty, omit them entirely. Do not include any other fields. Do not infer values from the presence of other fields. Do not interpret or guess.\n\nStrict selection rule:\n\n- Determine the payment method SOLELY from PaymentMethod. Do NOT use creditCards or any other fields to decide the method.\n\nMap PaymentMethod to these human names exactly:\n\n- ORA_PURCHASE_ORDER → Purchase order\n- ORA_WIRE → Wire\n\nInclude method-specific details ONLY when the PaymentMethod matches and the detail exists:\n\n- Purchase order: include PONumber only if PaymentMethod = ORA_PURCHASE_ORDER and PONumber exists (e.g., \"PO number PO12345\").\n- Wire: include WireNumber only if PaymentMethod = ORA_WIRE and WireNumber exists (e.g., \"Wire reference 98765\").\n- For Cash or Check, include no extra details.\n\nFormatting:\n\n- One sentence. No bullets. No code formatting. Human-friendly names only. No expiry dates.\n\nStructure: \"Payment method for {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHOD.$output.ProductName}} has been updated to [Human Payment Method Name][ with specific detail if present].\" If the method is unknown, use: \"Payment method for {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHOD.$output.ProductName}} has been updated.\"\n\nValidation:\n\n- Use only values present in {{$context.$nodes.UPDATE_SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT_METHOD.$output}}. Exclude any field that is null or empty. Do not add or infer anything.\n- Ensure the chosen method is strictly the one from PaymentMethod; do not switch to Credit card unless.\n\nExample with your sample data (do not copy values unless present at runtime):\n\n- PaymentMethod = ORA_PURCHASE_ORDER and PONumber = PO12345 → \"Payment method for Supremo Power Monitoring - Commercial has been updated to Purchase order (PO number PO12345).\""
            }
          ],
