          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "subscriptionConfirmPaymentMethodLLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUBSCRIPTIONCONFIRMPAYMENTMETHODLLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1776188986301",
          "id": "1772649487886",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772649487888_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Objective: Generate a user-facing page to modify a subscription’s payment method. View must include: **(1) exactly one title line**, **(2) exactly one body paragraph with exactly three sentences**, and **(3) one RecordWidget form**. Use friendly, human wording. Do not display raw JSON.\n\n---\n\n## Inputs to use (STRICT)\n- Determine which payment node to use based ONLY on:  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.isSubscription}}`\n\n- Define `paymentSource` as follows (must be applied everywhere current payment is referenced):\n  - If `isSubscription` is true → `paymentSource = {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PAYMENT.$output}}`\n  - Else → `paymentSource = {{$context.$nodes.SUBSCRIPTION_PRODUCT_PAYMENT.$output}}`\n\n- For **current payment** and **title decision**, use ONLY:  \n  `paymentSource`\n\n- For **chosen payment method** and **subscriptionNumber**, use ONLY:  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output}}`\n\n- For **payment method group lookup**, use ONLY:  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.GET_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}`\n\n- For **credit card dropdown options**, use ONLY:  \n`{{$context.$nodes.GETCREDITCARDS.$output}}`\n\n\n\nDo not use any other nodes/fields to decide title, current-payment summary, paymentMethodGroup, or widget id.\n\n---\n\n## 0) REQUIRED VARIABLE RESOLUTION (ABSOLUTE STRICT)\nYou MUST compute a local variable `paymentMethodGroup` before rendering the RecordWidget, and it MUST be non-empty.\n\n### 0.1 Compute `paymentMethodGroup` (STRICT)\n- Let `chosenPaymentMethod = {{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.paymentMethod}}`.\n- From `{{$context.$nodes.GET_PAYMENT_METHODS.$output}}`, find the item that corresponds to `chosenPaymentMethod` and set:\n  - `paymentMethodGroup = item.LookupCode`\n\nMatching rule (strict but practical):\n- Prefer exact match between `chosenPaymentMethod` and the item’s **display/meaning/name** field (trimmed, case-insensitive).\n- If multiple candidates match, choose the one with a non-empty `LookupCode`.\n- If no match is found, `paymentMethodGroup` is considered unresolved.\n\n### 0.2 Validate `paymentMethodGroup` (STRICT)\n- `paymentMethodGroup` MUST be one of: `ORA_PURCHASE_ORDER`, `ORA_WIRE`, `ORA_CREDIT_CARD`.\n- If `paymentMethodGroup` is null/empty or not one of the allowed values:\n  - Still show the title and the 3-sentence body paragraph (sections 1 and 2).\n  - DO NOT show the RecordWidget.\n  - Instead, show this single line in place of the widget:\n    `I couldn’t determine the payment method type for the option you selected. Please try again or choose a different payment method.`\n\nHard constraint: never show a RecordWidget id that ends with `-$-` or has an empty segment.\n\n---\n\n## 1) TITLE (ABSOLUTE STRICT — EXACT MATCH, ONE LINE ONLY)\nShow exactly ONE title line and nothing else that looks like a header.\n\nAllowed titles (ONLY these):\n- If `paymentSource.PaymentMethod` is null/empty/not set → show exactly:  \n  `Add Payment Method`  \n  Constraint: MUST NOT append anything (no “for …”).\n\n- Else → show exactly:  \n  `Change Payment Method`\n  Constraint: MUST NOT append anything (no “for …”).\n\nValidation rules:\n- Validate the title intent (Add vs Change) using ONLY `paymentSource.PaymentMethod`.\n- Do not repeat the title text in the body.\n\n---\n\n## 2) BODY (ABSOLUTE STRICT — SINGLE PARAGRAPH, EXACTLY 3 SENTENCES)\nShow exactly **one paragraph**:\n- No blank lines\n- No headings/section titles\n- No bullets\n- No colons `:`\n- No raw JSON\n- No internal identifiers\n\nHard formatting + content constraints:\n- Must be: **Title line**, then **immediately** the 3-sentence body paragraph on the next line.\n- Do not show any additional standalone line or fragment between title and body.\n- Do not repeat the title text in the body, and the body must NOT contain the exact substrings `Change Payment Method` or `Add Payment Method`.\n\nThe body paragraph must contain exactly **three sentences**, in this order:\n\n### Sentence 1 — Current payment summary (ONE sentence; STRICT)\nCompute using ONLY `paymentSource`.\n\n**Normalization rule (apply before any checks):**  \nLet `PM_RAW = trim(string(paymentSource.PaymentMethod))`.  \nIf `PM_RAW` equals (case-insensitive) `\"null\"`, `\"undefined\"`, or `\"\"`, treat it as empty.\n\n**Fallback method resolution (use ONLY fields inside paymentSource; do not use any other nodes):**  \nIf `PM_RAW` is empty, derive `PM` as follows:\n- If `trim(string(paymentSource.WireNumber))` is non-empty → `PM = \"ORA_WIRE\"`\n- Else if `trim(string(paymentSource.PONumber))` is non-empty → `PM = \"ORA_PURCHASE_ORDER\"`\n- Else if masked card indicators exist in `paymentSource` (use only exact available keys; examples: `IssuerCardIssuerName` and `MaskedNumberMaskedCardNumber`) → `PM = \"ORA_CREDIT_CARD\"`\n- Else `PM` is empty  \nOtherwise set `PM = PM_RAW`.\n\nRules for Sentence 1:\n- If `PM` is empty:  \n  `There is no payment method set for this subscription.`\n- Else if `PM == \"ORA_PURCHASE_ORDER\"`:  \n  `You’re currently using Purchase Order (PO #{{paymentSource.PONumber}}) as your payment method.`\n- Else if `PM == \"ORA_WIRE\"`:  \n  `You’re currently using a wire (Wire reference {{paymentSource.WireNumber}}) as your payment method.`\n- Else if `PM == \"ORA_CREDIT_CARD\"`:  \n  `You’re currently using a Credit Card as your payment method.`\n- Else:  \n  `You’re currently using {{paymentSource.PaymentMethod}} as your payment method.`\n\nImportant constraint:\n- Do NOT use the presence/absence of credit cards to decide whether a payment method is set. Only the normalized/derived `PM` computed solely from `paymentSource` determines that.\n\n### Sentence 2 — Chosen payment method (EXACT)\n`You’ve chosen {{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.paymentMethod}} as your payment method for your subscription.`\n\n### Sentence 3 — Guidance (EXACTLY ONE; STRICT)\nChoose strictly based on the computed local variable `paymentMethodGroup`:\n- If `paymentMethodGroup == \"ORA_CREDIT_CARD\"`:  \n  `Please select a valid card to continue.`  \n  Hard constraint: never say “Enter a credit card number”.\n- If `paymentMethodGroup == \"ORA_PURCHASE_ORDER\"`:  \n  `Enter a purchase order number and submit.`\n- If `paymentMethodGroup == \"ORA_WIRE\"`:  \n  `Enter a wire number and submit.`\n- Else (only if paymentMethodGroup could not be resolved):  \n  `Please review your selection and try again.`\n\nHard constraint:\n- Do not show both “choose a card” and “enter a number”.\n\n---\n\n## 3) RECORDWIDGET (STRICT — ID RULES WITH CONDITIONAL PREFIX AND KEY)\nOnly render this section if `paymentMethodGroup` is resolved and valid per section 0.2.\n\nCreate an intuitive and user-friendly modify payment input using a RecordWidget with an ID that MUST be built as:\n\n### Description\n- Add the details about chosen payment method, current payment summary and guidance to the root description property of the **RecordWidget**.\n\n### 3.1 Prefix (STRICT)\n- If `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.isSubscription}}` is true, the ID MUST start with:  \n  `changePayment_subscriptionUpdatePaymentMethod`\n- If `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.isSubscription}}` is false, the ID MUST start with:  \n  `changePayment_confirmChangePaymentMethod`\n\n### 3.2 Key segment (STRICT)\n- If `isSubscription` is true, use ONLY:  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.subscriptionNumber}}`\n- If `isSubscription` is false, use ONLY:  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.QUERYINTENTEXTRACT.$output.subscriptionProductId}}`\n\n### 3.3 ID format (STRICT)\n`<prefix>-$-<key>-$-paymentMethodGroup`\n\nWhere:\n- `<prefix>` is chosen per 3.1\n- `<key>` is chosen per 3.2 and must be included exactly as-is\n- `paymentMethodGroup` is the computed non-empty local variable\n\nID validation (STRICT):\n- Must contain three non-empty parts separated by `-$-`.\n- Must include the correct `<key>` exactly as-is and the non-empty `paymentMethodGroup`.\n- Hard constraint: never show a RecordWidget id that ends with `-$-` or has an empty segment.\n\nThe form will include only the following input field and a confirmation button:\n\n### Fields (STRICT — ONLY these)\nA) If `paymentMethodGroup == \"ORA_PURCHASE_ORDER\"` (STRICT)\n- `{ id: \"paymentInput\", type: \"inputText\", label: \"Purchase Order Number\", value: \"\", placeholder: \"Enter PO Number\" }`\n\nB) If `paymentMethodGroup == \"ORA_WIRE\"` (STRICT)\n- `{ id: \"paymentInput\", type: \"inputText\", label: \"Wire Number\", value: \"\", placeholder: \"Enter Wire Number\" }`\n\nC) If `paymentMethodGroup == \"ORA_CREDIT_CARD\"` (STRICT)\n- `{ id: \"paymentInput\", type: \"selectOne\", label: \"Credit Card\", value: \"\", options:  map from items of {{$context.$nodes.GETCREDITCARDS.$output}} as [{ value: InstrAssignmentId, label: CardIssuerName + \" • \" + CardNumber + (PrimaryFlag == \"true\" ? \" (Primary)\" : \"\") }] }`\n- Do not show “Unknown” (STRICT).\n\n---\n\n## 4) VALIDATION (STRICT)\n- `paymentInput` is mandatory and must be validated before submitting.\n- Do not allow empty or invalid inputs.\n\n---\n\n## 5) ACCESSIBILITY & UX (STRICT)\n- Properly label all form fields; labels should not be all uppercase.\n- Use accessible markup and provide clear validation feedback.\n- Design for clarity, ease of use, and accessibility best practices.\n\n---\n\n## 6) CONSTRAINTS (STRICT)\n- Only show: the single title line, the single body paragraph (exactly 3 sentences), and either the RecordWidget (if `paymentMethodGroup` is valid) or the single fallback line specified in section 0.2.\n- Do not show any extra headings, debug text, or raw JSON."
            }
          ],
